37	  /**
38	   * Matches strings that contain {@code .} or {@code ..} as a complete path segment. This also
39	   * matches dots in their percent-encoded form, {@code %2E}.
40	   *
41	   * <p>It is okay to have these strings within a larger path segment (like {@code a..z} or {@code
42	   * index.html}) but when alone they have a special meaning. A single dot resolves to no path
43	   * segment so {@code /one/./three/} becomes {@code /one/three/}. A double-dot pops the preceding
44	   * directory, so {@code /one/../three/} becomes {@code /three/}.
